W44-168 (Smart-Zenjxl chunk 5, 2026-05-21) — adaptive butteraugli_iters per image content
===========================================================================================

Status: [HONEST-STOP — API + env hook + helpers SHIPPED as forward-compat;
         production default Mode A = byte-identical to pre-W44-168 main]

W44-163 Smart-Zenjxl audit A2 pick. Per user directive 2026-05-21:
*"make zenjxl defaults smarter on the rdtime axis, to know where to spend
resources by image for compression per effort level, even if effort levels
blend together more"*.

The fixed per-effort `butteraugli_iters` schedule (`e≤7 → 0, e8 → 2,
e9 → 4, e10 → 8, e11 → 16, e12 → 32`) is intrinsically content-agnostic
— smooth photos / screenshots at e8+ converge after fewer iters AND
textured content at e7 (which currently runs ZERO iters) could benefit
from a small budget. W44-168 wires three content-aware adjustment modes
gated on cheap proxies already on hand (`mask1x1_median`, `mask1x1_p25`,
`edge_density`).

Mechanism layer: BUTTLOOP ITERATION COUNT — a NEW layer not touched by
W44-164/166/167. Designed to COMPOSE with all prior Smart-Zenjxl chunks
(unlike W44-165's competing-mechanism layer issue or W44-167's
same-table-layer competition with W44-166).

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes (env hook `JXL_W44_168_MODE=A|B|C|D`, default A unset)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

A — Baseline: byte-identical to fixed schedule. Production default.

B — SmoothSkip: at `effort >= 8` on smooth/screenshot content
    (`mask1x1_median > 95` OR `mask1x1_p25 >= 85`), `iters - 1`
    saturating at 1. Saves one full buttloop iter on converged content.

C — TexturedExtend: at `effort == 7` on textured content
    (`edge_density >= 0.5`), bump iters from 0 → 2. Blends e7 upward
    toward e8 quality.

D — Combined: B and C together (mutually exclusive on the effort axis).

------------------------------------------------------------------------
